# SABOTAGE: B-OBAN adoption seam — neuters `Samen.Jobs.install_default_queues/1`'s
# BACKFILL so a host-declared `queues:` list is returned unchanged instead of being
# merged with the canonical taxonomy. This is the pre-fix world restored: any host that
# hand-lists queues silently loses every canonical queue it forgot (which is how all four
# shipped hosts ended up without `:webhooks_in`, and three without `:automation` /
# `:automation_timers`). The failure mode is invisible at runtime — the app boots, Oban
# reports healthy, and jobs on the dropped queues sit `available` forever. The seam's
# merge semantics are therefore load-bearing, not cosmetic: the named tests must FAIL.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/jobs_queue_parity_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: install_default_queues/1 BACKFILLS a host list that omits canonical queues
# MUST_FAIL: install_default_queues/1 preserves a host's deliberate limit override
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/jobs.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/jobs.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/jobs.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/jobs.ex
@@ -293,12 +293,7 @@
 
   # Host-declared limits win; every canonical queue the host omitted is appended.
   defp merge_queues(host_queues) do
-    missing =
-      Enum.reject(default_queue_config(), fn {name, _limit} ->
-        Keyword.has_key?(host_queues, name)
-      end)
-
-    host_queues ++ missing
+    host_queues
   end
 
   @doc """
